TYPES.md §3.7, CODEGEN.md §2.1: a malformed `mode` (a string, or an unknown mode) or a malformed `values` is E8009 alone: such an emit selects no let, so a public let of a local type there is not E2111 too.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Stone {
  n: Int
}

/// The stones.
let stones: [Stone] = []

emit go { out: "@sovcommon/a", mode: "types" }

emit cpp { out: "@sovcommon/a", mode: bogus }

emit ts { out: "@sovcommon/a.ts", values: stones }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8009]  a/a.canon:10:38
  option mode of emit go must be a mode name

error[E8009]  a/a.canon:12:39
  invalid mode bogus for emit cpp: expected one of baked, embedded, data, types

error[E8009]  a/a.canon:14:43
  option values of emit ts must be a list of value names

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
